  "body": "I'm trying to create a direct chat for 2 users - user1 and user2 with API.\r\n\r\n1) I create a room as user1 and invite user2, get $room_id:\r\ncurl -X POST --header 'Content-Type: application/json' --header 'Accept: application/json' -d '{  \"creation_content\": {   \r\n \"invite\": [\"@user2:domain.local\"],   \r\n  \"is_direct\": \"true\",\r\n  \"preset\": \"trusted_private_chat\",\r\n   \"visibility\": \"private\" }' 'http://localhost:8008/_matrix/client/unstable/createRoom?access_token=$user1_token'\r\n\r\n2) I accept the invitation to the room on behalf of user2:\r\ncurl -XPOST -d '{}' http://localhost:8008/_matrix/client/r0/rooms/$room_id/join?access_token=$user2_token\"\r\n\r\n\r\nIn user2, the room is marked as Direct Messages, but in user1 as a group chat. How to fix it? user1 should also be like Direct Messages\r\n",
